# `lib/` is no longer ignored: forge-std is a git submodule, so git stores a gitlink rather than
# its contents. Ignoring the directory would make a fresh clone build without forge-std, which is
# exactly the failure converting it to a submodule was meant to remove. Git cannot re-include a
# path whose parent directory is excluded, so the rule has to go rather than be negated.
